---
source: tests/golden.rs
---
  x `core/tools` installs packages, and repo.kdl denies the package step the
  | network
  help: set `packages "allow"` in repo.kdl's `security-policy { network }`, or
        leave this module out of the image

  x `core/fetcher` declares that its scripts reach the network, and repo.kdl
  | denies it
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-network/modules/core/fetcher/module.kdl:7:1]
 6 | 
 7 | network "scripts"
   : ^^^|^^^
   :    `-- denied by `scripts "deny"`
 8 | 
   `----
  help: set `scripts "strict"` in repo.kdl's `security-policy { network }` to
        honour this declaration, or leave this module out of the image

  x `core/asset-only` declares an asset its script step cannot fetch
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-network/modules/core/asset-only/module.kdl:7:1]
 6 | 
 7 | asset "tool" {
   : ^^|^^
   :   `-- fetched with the network closed
 8 |     pin {
   `----
  help: set `scripts "strict"` in repo.kdl's `security-policy { network }` and
        declare `network "scripts"`, or leave this module out of the image

  x `core/fragment-only` declares a script step it has not got
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-network/modules/core/fragment-only/module.kdl:7:1]
 6 | 
 7 | network "scripts"
   : ^^^|^^^
   :    `-- no standard layer
 8 | 
   `----
  help: `standard-layer #false` leaves the fragment the only thing this module
        emits, and a fragment's own RUN lines are emitted as written

  x `core/installer` installs packages in module.sh, and its script step has
  | no network
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-network/modules/core/installer/module.kdl:1:1]
 1 | schema-version 1
   : ^
   : `-- `dnf5` needs the network
 2 | 
   `----
  help: set `scripts "strict"` in repo.kdl's `security-policy { network }` and
        declare `network "scripts"`, or leave this module out of the image
